# Postgres connection URL for the live store. When set (env or this file),
# _db()/confirmations/plan-approvals route through world/db_backend.py
# instead of the SQLite file; an explicit THINK_TANK_DB override still wins
# (tests, operator redirects). DSN example:
# postgresql://user@/dbname (local unix socket, trust auth).
THINK_TANK_DB_URL=
# Set to 1 to run this process as the read-only replica (serve.py
# --read-only): reads come from the shared store, writes are refused with
# 405, and the background loops / sim do not start. The primary process
# (com.austtp.ai-think-tank) must never set this.
THINK_TANK_READ_ONLY=
# Test-process sandbox switch (tests/conftest.py sets it): db_backend forces
# the SQLite path and never resolves the THINK_TANK_DB_URL DSN, so a test
